o try to  muscle through and do without so i think  the concept has a lot of potential and  makes a lot of sense i mean i'm all for  encouraging folks to eat their veg but  not if your meals leave you hangry and  sad you're not a child you are a grown  ass adult and if forcing yourself to eat  foods that you do not like makes you  unhappy or hungry you're gonna rebel  you're gonna snap and you're likely  going to eventually binge and that's not  the only questionable post i've seen  lately that has raised some eyebrows  especially since some of them seem to  contradict her earlier more gentle  posts so this one for example about  throwing junk food away because wasting  actual food is apparently better than  the possibility of carrying body fat  yeah it felt elitist and inadvertently  fat phobic in my opinion now maybe she's  on her own body journey right now and  maybe this militant tough love approach  works for her  are you ready to work  are you ready to work but research  suggests it's not appropriate for most  people and it's absolutely not without  risks so in conclusion well i respect a  wide range of clinical approaches and  i'm confident that elana's program  specifically has helped a number of  people lose weight it's not going to be  for everyone especially for a lot of you  who i know need a much more gentle  approach i think the core of the 2b  program makes absolute sense and has the  potential to help support a more  balanced lifestyle for weight management  but it can also be very risky without  proper flexibility customization and a  strong relationship with food so on that  note that is all that i have for you  guys today if you like this video please  feel free to give it the thumbs up leave  me a comment below with your thoughts on  the program or other weight loss  programs that you want to see me review  subscribe to the channel and i will see  you next time on abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

